The website must feel respectful and contemporary. It must not feel frightening, excessively religious, clinical, cheap, or like a generic funeral-services directory.

Design direction

Primary background: warm ivory or off-white.

Main text: deep charcoal.

Supporting surfaces: soft beige and light neutral gray.

Accent: muted sage or restrained forest green.

Optional secondary accent: subtle warm bronze.

Typography: a readable modern sans-serif, with a refined heading style.

Generous whitespace.

Clear product photography.

Subtle borders and understated shadows.

Consistent spacing, radii, buttons, and form elements.

Smooth, restrained transitions.

Accessible contrast and visible keyboard focus.

Avoid excessive animations, dramatic imagery, black-heavy layouts, large decorative crosses, religious symbols used indiscriminately, and aggressive promotional banners.

Use original brand assets or properly licensed imagery. Never use an image merely because it depicts a product category if the actual product or ritual is materially different.

Create a simple LastCry wordmark with a restrained, memorable symbol if appropriate. Keep the logo text readable at mobile sizes.

Use real product imagery wherever possible. If the project starts without assets, use clearly identified temporary placeholders and document the replacement process.

The visual quality should be comparable to a carefully designed modern specialty e-commerce brand.

